Each capability task includes its own abuse/failure tests. Security debt does not get deferred to Task 073.", "v0.2 — Independent Android, remote control and sync
Apply `architecture/android_operating_model.lcl.txt` A3–A8 at the time each capability is built.
- Phone-local tool execution enforces scoped roots, user-granted storage access, permissions, secret isolation and auditability without relying on the PC.
- Account authentication, local device unlock, provider authentication and remote pairing are separate authorities. Pairing does not export stored credentials or grant unrestricted shell access.
- Use authenticated encrypted transport and revocable peer trust from the first network-capable task; never defer it to final hardening.
- Scope commands/approvals to their exact target/revision and expiration; handle lost acknowledgments without duplicate side effects.
- Exclude secrets, MFA recovery material and private device trust keys from ordinary workspace sync. Reconcile permission-changing actions separately, never by merging editable files.
- Verify incoming file paths, schemas, sizes, revisions and peer authority before applying changes; incoming LCL is untrusted until validated/adopted.
- Local-only files stay local unless the user explicitly selects synchronization or a model operation requiring their transmission.", "v0.3 — Import and model-switch boundaries
