Use one primary Nexees implementation agent. Do not spawn subagents, delegated AI reviewers, background AI jobs or recursive model calls under this profile.
An independently owner-started Codex session working on Arch Dock in the same VS Code window is not a Claude-spawned agent and is not a Nexees violation. Leave that repository, its task/evidence files and its running processes alone.
Nexees-started heavy builds/tests/emulators/local models remain sequential. Respect real resource pressure; do not launch competing heavy work or terminate another session to free resources. Another owner-authorized session is not grounds to repeatedly demand permission for lightweight Nexees work.
A hook message naming another repository/commit is not evidence of a Nexees defect and grants no permission to inspect, scan or modify that other project. Record the mismatch briefly and continue if it is non-blocking and demonstrably unrelated. If the hook actually blocks this task or attempts unauthorized side effects, report that exact blocker without disabling/bypassing the safeguard or supplying credentials.

CA-10 — Interrupt only for a real decision or boundary
Ask once with the smallest relevant facts and proposed bounded next action when: the required owner preference is unanswered; authority/identity/ownership is unresolved; an in-scope repair cannot restore a required gate; credentials/OS consent/human observation are indispensable; a resource/cost limit or explicit stop is reached; or continuation would cross scope, a security boundary or remote-history safety.
Do not ask again for permissions already granted by this profile or a still-applicable owner instruction. Record granted decisions for the authorized scope. Persist status and exact next action on a genuine stop.
DESKTOP-RENDERER-01 remains the owner's decision at TASK-003 before renderer-dependent selection. Do not invent the choice, ask for it during unrelated TASK-002 work, or treat a synthetic fixture as the answer. Any other unresolved asset/license/platform decision is raised only when it actually blocks the assigned task.
Continue only unaffected work still within the current task's authorization, not an unassigned later task. A blocker is never waived merely to reduce interruptions.

CA-11 — Concise communication and mid-session continuation
Mid-session messages state only the next action, permission or blocker-resolution decision. Existing package rules stay in force without repetition. Restate a rule only for an explicit change, exception or conflict.
Completion reports give: task/acceptance status; verification summary and evidence location; commit/sync status; and a real unresolved blocker if any. Put detailed receipts, command logs and explanations in evidence files, not repeated chat essays or Insight sections.
For a user-authorized range, a short task checkpoint is informational; do not stop solely to wait for acknowledgment after every passing task. For a single named task, stop after its accepted/committed/synced completion or report a genuine incomplete stage honestly.

CA-12 — Deferred scope is still deferred
Keep exactly 75 numbered tasks. Do not add Windows/macOS/other-distribution release obligations or otherwise expand the product plan through this workflow revision.
The previously agreed optional Review/Supervisor feature remains a TASK-075 amendment, to be integrated and tested at that stage before the final bug-fixing/regression/release pass. This profile is procedural authorization for the existing primary coding agent, not implementation of that Supervisor, and does not enable a reviewer agent now.
TASK-075 still needs all mandatory real release evidence and the owner's explicit public release/publication authorization. Candidate validation, local acceptance and normal Git sync do not themselves publish a release.
